// What this compiler reports as its version.
//
// ⭐⭐ **THESE ARE DEFAULTS, AND THE BUILD REPLACES THEM WITH `--define`.** `build.maxon` derives the
// real values from git and passes them as `Compiler.CompilerVersion` and its two siblings; nothing
// rewrites this file, and a build never dirties the working tree.
//
// ⛔ **IT IS TRACKED SOURCE AND MUST STAY THAT WAY.** It used to be generated by `build.maxon`, which
// could not work on a fresh checkout: generating it needs a compiler, and the compiler cannot be built
// without it. A clone had no `CompilerVersion` at all and every lane failed to compile. A default that
// is honest — `dev`, built from an unknown commit — makes the file self-sufficient, and `--define` is
// what a build with more to say uses to say it.
//
// The shape is rustc's: `maxon 0.1.1 (a1b2c3d 2026-09-09)`. A release number alone cannot answer a bug
// report about "0.1.1" when there have been forty builds of it; the commit and the day can.
export let CompilerVersion = "dev"
export let CompilerCommit = "unknown"
export let CompilerCommitDate = "unknown"
